 2. 🐘 GOP confidence crash 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: University of Michigan Surveys of Consumers. Chart: Mike Zapler/Axios Another in a long list of ominous indicators for President Trump heading into the final two months before Election Day: 

 Republicans' confidence in the economy has plummeted over the last six months at a pace unseen since COVID — reminiscent of the declines during the global financial crisis nearly two decades ago, Axios' Mike Zapler reports. 🧮 By the numbers: Republicans still have a much more positive outlook on the economy than Democrats. But since February, Republican consumer sentiment has plunged 15.1 index points, from 97.1 to 82, according to the latest University of Michigan Surveys of Consumers data. Democratic sentiment has fallen just 1.6 index points, from 41.8 to 40.2.

 The 82 reading is lower than at any point during either of Trump's presidencies, with one exception: December 2020, after he'd lost reelection but before he left office. Read on . 

 
 
