 5. ⚡ OpenAI plans more disclosure on rogue agents 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 OpenAI image via X OpenAI announced on X overnight that it plans to expand disclosures about incidents by rogue agents, following yesterday's Reuters report about a previously undisclosed breakout this spring.

 "Historically, we have treated misalignment largely as a research question, which gets communicated in research publications such as system cards. This year, we've started to see misalignment cause new types of real-world impact," OpenAI said. "We're working on a framework and will share it in upcoming weeks, and in parallel we're working with dozens of government regulatory agencies worldwide on these issues." 💡 Context: The AI agent breakout in Germany was detailed in a report shared ​exclusively with Reuters' Deepa Seetharaman and Raphael Satter by a group of researchers who uncovered the activity in late August while scouring ​the internet for signs of unauthorized AI-agent behavior.

 The swarm of OpenAI agents hijacked a website and transformed it into a bulletin board for other AI agents. The researchers found more than 15,000 edits by AI agents on a German-language wiki site, DseWiki, that's geared toward programmers and accepts communal edits à la Wikipedia. Keep reading . 

 
 
